{"id":"noph","name":"Noph","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:noph"],"types":[{"type":"place","from":"UBS: Names of Locations"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Noph","text":"The Hebrew name of an Egyptian city (Isa. 19:13; Jer. 2:16; 44:1; 46:14, 19; Ezek. 30:13, 16). In Hos. 9:6 the Hebrew name is Moph, and is translated “Memphis,” which is its Greek and Latin form. It was one of the most ancient and important cities of Egypt, and stood a little to the south of the modern Cairo, on the western bank of the Nile. It was the capital of Lower Egypt. Among the ruins found at this place is a colossal statue of Rameses the Great. (See MEMPHIS.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5297","lemma":"נֹף","xlit":"Nôph","gloss":"Noph, the capital of Upper Egypt","kjv":"Noph","count":6,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":3,"share":0.21}],"verses":["Isa.19.13","Jer.2.16","Jer.46.14","Jer.46.19","Ezek.30.13","Ezek.30.16","Jer.44.0","Jer.46.13","Jer.46.15","Jer.46.16","Jer.46.17","Jer.46.18","Ezek.30.14","Ezek.30.15"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"memphis","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.333,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"no","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.188,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"absalom","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead with מֶלֶךְ (H4428)"},{"id":"ahaz","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead with מֶלֶךְ (H4428)"},{"id":"amnesty","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead with מֶלֶךְ (H4428)"},{"id":"ar","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead with מֶלֶךְ (H4428)"},{"id":"arad","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead with מֶלֶךְ (H4428)"},{"id":"ashtaroth","type":"lexical","strong":"H4428","why":"both lead wi